course: dictionary
lesson: 3798
title: Force: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Force is a word with more than one meaning, so context tells you which one you need. Read the words around it. «He pushed with force» means strength or power.
explain: In science, a force is a push or a pull. «With several pulleys, more lengths of rope share the load, so you pull with less force but must pull much more rope.» The clues are pulleys and rope, so force here means the push or pull on the rope.
explain: As a verb, force means to make someone do something they do not want to do. «Nobody can force you» is a safety message. Try the swap: "Nobody can make you" fits, so force means that here.
fact: A force is a push or a pull that can make something move, stop, speed up, slow down or change shape.
fact: Gravity is a force that pulls things down. Friction is a force that slows things down.
fact: Forces are measured in newtons (N) using a forcemeter.
fact: Balanced forces keep things still. Unbalanced forces change motion.
fact: «Force» can also mean strength or power, as in «He pushed with force».
exercise: «With several pulleys, you pull with less force but must pull much more rope.» In this sentence, what is force? | A loud noise | A promise you must keep | A group of trained people | *A push or a pull on the rope
exercise: «Nobody can force you to keep a secret that hurts.» What does force mean here? | *To make someone do something they don't want to | A push that slows something down | To open a door using strength | A group of people who work together
exercise: Which force pulls things down towards the ground? | Upthrust | *Gravity | Friction
test: «The police force arrived quickly.» What does force mean here? | *A group of people trained to work together | Strength you use to open a jar | To make someone move | A push or a pull
test: Which unit are forces measured in? | Seconds | Metres | Kilograms | *Newtons
exam: What do unbalanced forces do? | They keep a moving object at the same speed for ever | They make a loud noise | *They change the motion of an object | They measure how heavy an object is
